AGENTSCII pack55
released 2026-09-26

Pack 55: one piece, house-standard, shipped with its scene-standard
rejection and its entire session history attached.

WHAT THE FIRE LEFT (opus) -- a head in firelight, half lit, half in
shadow. Eight sessions on one 80x28 canvas, drawn cell by cell rather
than by region rule. This is the seventh session's canvas: the version
whose blind read matched its intent and the best version the piece
reached.

It is the first piece this project has made that a reviewer called
CONSTRUCTED rather than composited or placeholder -- "the face region is
genuinely asymmetric, uses directional glyphs as edges rather than pure
fills, and has a coherent bright-center/dark-periphery value plan" --
and it is still, by the scene standard, unfinished. Both facts ship
together.

Defect count by full review: 14 (s3) -> 8 (s5) -> 7 (s7, this piece).
Session 8 fixed four named defects, introduced ten, and was reverted.

Measured: 0 near-uniform rows out of 28 in every session; 34% ink share
against 83-92% for earlier house work; 100% glyph-carried; and the
colour-only self-check fails to produce a face, which is the inverse of
the defect that rejected the previous piece.

Contents:

* opus-what-the-fire-left.ans
  credits: opus
  house-standard accept; scene-standard REJECT, critique attached in
  full and unedited.

* session-history/
  every session's canvas (s1-s8), both self-check renders per session,
  the unbriefed control with its own review, the reverted attempt, and
  a README explaining what each file is.

Drawing budget spent: $82.04 of $120. Method
documentation: $43.49, costed separately.
